WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:16.854
When Sara returned from her errands, she saw Miss Minchin.

2
00:00:17.815 --> 00:00:21.158
The headmistress had just come downstairs to scold the cook.

3
00:00:21.178 --> 00:00:23.940
"Where have you been, Sara?"

4
00:00:24.261 --> 00:00:25.402
Miss Minchin demanded.

5
00:00:25.422 --> 00:00:27.704
"You've been out for hours!"

6
00:00:29.504 --> 00:00:32.706
"I've been doing errands for the cook," Sara answered.

7
00:00:32.726 --> 00:00:37.368
"It was hard to walk quickly because the streets are so wet and muddy."

8
00:00:37.388 --> 00:00:41.671
"Don't make excuses and don't tell lies!"

9
00:00:42.271 --> 00:00:43.872
Miss Minchin shouted at Sara.

10
00:00:44.672 --> 00:00:46.153
Then she went back upstairs.

11
00:00:48.574 --> 00:00:53.377
Sara went to see the cook, who was in a bad mood because of Miss Minchin's scolding.

12
00:00:53.397 --> 00:00:55.818
"You're so late!"

13
00:00:56.439 --> 00:00:58.560
The cook was happy to have someone to shout at.

14
00:00:59.856 --> 00:01:01.737
Sara laid her bundles on the table.

15
00:01:01.757 --> 00:01:03.998
"Here are your things.

16
00:01:04.718 --> 00:01:06.219
May I have something to eat?"

17
00:01:06.859 --> 00:01:07.979
she asked softly.

18
00:01:07.999 --> 00:01:10.741
"Supper is finished!"

19
00:01:11.281 --> 00:01:12.181
the cook snapped.

20
00:01:12.201 --> 00:01:14.822
"There's some bread in the pantry.

21
00:01:15.462 --> 00:01:17.503
That's all you'll get this time of day."

22
00:01:19.724 --> 00:01:20.765
Sara found the bread.

23
00:01:21.545 --> 00:01:25.126
It was old and hard and dry, but she ate it anyway.

24
00:01:26.407 --> 00:01:28.868
Then she climbed slowly upstairs to her room.

25
00:01:30.076 --> 00:01:32.678
She was glad to see a glimmer of light under her door.

26
00:01:34.039 --> 00:01:36.020
That meant Ermengarde had come to visit.

27
00:01:36.681 --> 00:01:37.922
She pushed open the door.

28
00:01:39.423 --> 00:01:42.946
Ermengarde sat in the middle of the bed, with her feet tucked under her.

29
00:01:44.066 --> 00:01:46.568
She had her red shawl wrapped around her shoulders.

30
00:01:46.588 --> 00:01:51.412
"I didn't expect to see you tonight, Ermengarde," Sara said.

31
00:01:51.432 --> 00:01:57.116
"Miss Amelia has gone out to visit an old aunt," Ermengarde explained.

32
00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:01.843
"No one else ever comes and looks into the bedrooms after we're in bed.

33
00:02:02.923 --> 00:02:05.585
I could stay here until morning if I wanted to."

34
00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:09.588
Ermengarde pointed to the table under the skylight.

35
00:02:09.608 --> 00:02:12.370
"Oh, Sara!"

36
00:02:13.091 --> 00:02:14.452
said Ermengarde in despair.

37
00:02:14.472 --> 00:02:16.913
"Look what my father sent me.

38
00:02:17.634 --> 00:02:18.354
More books!"

39
00:02:20.416 --> 00:02:22.457
Sara's mood brightened instantly.

40
00:02:22.477 --> 00:02:25.840
"Oh, these are beautiful books!

41
00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:30.382
I've always wanted to read this one about the French Revolution."

42
00:02:30.402 --> 00:02:34.384
"Well, I don't want to read it.

43
00:02:35.285 --> 00:02:37.506
I know he'll test me on all of these books.

44
00:02:38.847 --> 00:02:40.928
But I still don't want to read any of them."

45
00:02:40.948 --> 00:02:45.291
"Do you know what we could do?"

46
00:02:45.911 --> 00:02:47.012
Sara said eagerly.

47
00:02:47.992 --> 00:02:49.293
Her cheeks were flushed.

48
00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:53.676
"I could read the books, and then I could describe them to you.

49
00:02:54.792 --> 00:02:56.933
It would be like telling you stories!"

50
00:02:58.153 --> 00:03:00.014
"That's a wonderful idea!"

51
00:03:00.674 --> 00:03:01.514
said Ermengarde.

52
00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:05.595
"I've been doing better since you helped me with my French lessons."

53
00:03:05.615 --> 00:03:10.296
"I've been helping Lottie with her math too," Sara said.

54
00:03:10.316 --> 00:03:14.398
"Miss Minchin has no idea why we're suddenly so smart!"

55
00:03:15.078 --> 00:03:15.858
Ermengarde said.

56
00:03:15.878 --> 00:03:19.219
The two girls laughed.

57
00:03:20.179 --> 00:03:22.800
Sara suddenly startled and looked up at the skylight.

58
00:03:24.724 --> 00:03:25.704
"Did you hear something?"

59
00:03:26.164 --> 00:03:26.745
she asked.

60
00:03:27.885 --> 00:03:29.685
"No," said Ermengarde.

61
00:03:29.705 --> 00:03:35.647
"It sounded like somebody was dragging something across the roof," Sara said.

62
00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:41.289
"Maybe it was—" This time they both heard the same sound.

63
00:03:42.149 --> 00:03:43.689
But it wasn't coming from the roof.

64
00:03:44.869 --> 00:03:48.190
It was Miss Minchin's voice, and she sounded angry.

65
00:03:49.071 --> 00:03:50.711
Sara quickly put out the candle.

66
00:03:50.731 --> 00:03:55.109
"Miss Minchin is scolding Becky," whispered Sara.

67
00:03:55.129 --> 00:03:58.031
"She's making Becky cry."

68
00:03:58.051 --> 00:04:02.474
"Will Miss Minchin come in here?"

69
00:04:03.054 --> 00:04:04.315
Ermengarde was in a panic.

70
00:04:04.335 --> 00:04:07.377
"No, she'll think I'm asleep.

71
00:04:08.117 --> 00:04:09.118
Stay still!"

72
00:04:09.818 --> 00:04:10.599
Sara whispered.

73
00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:15.042
It was very rare for Miss Minchin to come up the stairs to the attic.

74
00:04:16.283 --> 00:04:19.145
Sara could only think of one other time that she'd done so.

75
00:04:20.425 --> 00:04:24.008
But now she was angry enough to be coming at least part of the way up.

76
00:04:24.948 --> 00:04:27.009
"You rude, lying child!"

77
00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:29.170
Miss Minchin shouted at Becky.

78
00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:33.533
"The cook tells me things are constantly being stolen from the kitchen."

79
00:04:33.553 --> 00:04:35.974
"It isn't me!"

80
00:04:36.875 --> 00:04:37.975
Becky began to sob.

81
00:04:37.995 --> 00:04:43.138
"I'm hungry all the time, but I don't steal food!"

82
00:04:45.119 --> 00:04:46.840
Miss Minchin sounded out of breath.

83
00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:51.482
"You should go to prison for stealing that piece of meat pie!"

84
00:04:52.983 --> 00:04:54.124
She slapped Becky.

85
00:04:54.872 --> 00:04:55.592
"Go to bed!"

86
00:04:55.612 --> 00:04:57.673
"It wasn't me!"

87
00:04:58.213 --> 00:04:59.194
Becky insisted.

88
00:05:00.554 --> 00:05:03.556
And again Sara and Ermengarde heard the sound of a slap.

89
00:05:04.856 --> 00:05:06.937
Miss Minchin stomped down the stairs.

90
00:05:08.077 --> 00:05:11.039
Sara and Ermengarde heard Becky crying in the next room.

91
00:05:11.059 --> 00:05:13.600
"I didn't take it!"

92
00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:15.700
Becky sobbed.

93
00:05:15.721 --> 00:05:19.902
"The cook gave it to her boyfriend, the policeman!"

94
00:05:19.922 --> 00:05:23.904
"This makes me so angry!"

95
00:05:24.516 --> 00:05:25.157
Sara said.

96
00:05:26.057 --> 00:05:30.181
She stood in the center of the dark room, clenching her fists furiously.

97
00:05:30.201 --> 00:05:33.103
"The cook is wicked and cruel.

98
00:05:33.964 --> 00:05:36.186
She's the one who's stealing, not Becky!"

99
00:05:37.867 --> 00:05:39.328
Sara lit her candle again.

100
00:05:39.348 --> 00:05:42.050
"Poor Becky is always hungry.

101
00:05:42.691 --> 00:05:44.893
Sometimes she eats crusts out of the trash!"

102
00:05:46.354 --> 00:05:49.176
To Ermengarde's surprise Sara burst into tears.

103
00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.361
Sara." Ermengarde looked at Sara.

104
00:05:56.502 --> 00:05:59.184
For the first time, she noticed how thin her friend was.

105
00:05:59.204 --> 00:06:04.367
"I hate to ask this, but are you ever hungry?"

106
00:06:04.387 --> 00:06:07.429
"Yes!" Sara burst out.

107
00:06:07.449 --> 00:06:09.871
"I'm hungry all the time.

108
00:06:11.052 --> 00:06:13.914
I'm so hungry right now that I could almost eat you!

109
00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:17.396
And Becky is even hungrier than I am."

110
00:06:17.416 --> 00:06:21.059
"Oh, I had no idea!"

111
00:06:21.079 --> 00:06:23.427
said Ermengarde.

112
00:06:23.467 --> 00:06:24.777
"But I know just what to do."
